    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily on speed-infusion today, with **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **Corbin Carroll** (75.70) serving as our strongest plays. **Mickey Moniak** benefits immensely from a soft matchup against G. Holmes, capitalizing on a favorable SP skill rating and dynamic platoon splits to lead our lineup in efficiency. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** continues to be a high-upside anchor; despite a slight park penalty, his elite profile in the #2 hole against Tidwell makes him a must-start as we hunt for stolen bases to maintain our categorical advantage. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants attention (74.00), as his plate discipline pairs perfectly with the slow delivery of Lowder, creating an optimal environment for him to exploit the basepaths.\n\nPlatoon edges are the primary catalyst for our mid-tier scoring, specifically for **Jose Caballero**, whose 71.34 rating is bolstered by a massive +13% platoon boost against Sandoval. Conversely, our toughest start is **Josh Naylor** (50.39), who faces the elite arm of Cease. While **Josh Naylor** clings to a starting spot, the proximity of **Cole Young** (35.86) on our bench highlights our strict adherence to the 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" **Cole Young** failed to make the cut due to the severe SP skill penalty posed by Cease, which dragged his projection well below the required threshold to justify burning a game cap. We are cautiously monitoring the lineup status for **Gabriel Moreno**, whose #3 spot provides necessary protection, though we must remain wary of any late-day weather shifts or lineup adjustments that could depress the value of our lower-score starters like **Isaac Paredes** (51.74) or **Travis Bazzana** (52.81) as they navigate their respective matchups.",
